---
import DemoLessonLayout from "../../../layouts/DemoLessonLayout.astro";
---

<DemoLessonLayout
  title="Try a private remote server"
  description="Run the same teaching server on a VM you control and reach it over a private network."
  downloads
  next={{ path: "labs/wireshark/", label: "Read a TCP capture" }}
>
  <section class="lab-section" aria-labelledby="private-server">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2 id="private-server" tabindex="-1">
        Run and verify the remote transfer
      </h2>
      <p>
        Use this extension to learn what changes when the server is on another
        network.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="lab-steps">
      <li>Put the teaching server on a VM you control with Python 3.</li>
      <li>
        Connect the VM and your laptop to a private network such as
        <a href="https://tailscale.com/docs/features/access-control">
          Tailscale
        </a>
        . Allow the demo laptop to reach port 5001 and keep it closed on the
        public interface.
      </li>
      <li>
        Start the server with{" "}
        <code>python3 server.py --host VM_PRIVATE_IP</code>. On your laptop,
        send HELLO with
        <code>python3 client.py hello.txt --host VM_PRIVATE_IP</code>.
        Substitute the VM’s private address in both commands.
      </li>
      <li>
        Check the application’s OK reply and compare the file hashes on the two
        machines. Stop the listener after the rehearsal.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <details>
      <summary>Verify which address is reachable</summary>
      <p>
        Compare the listener’s starting message with the destination in the
        client command. Both should show the VM’s private address and port 5001.
        Run the same transfer on loopback first if you need to isolate an
        application problem from a network problem.
      </p>
    </details>
    <p>
      <strong>Check your work.</strong> Your authorized laptop gets an OK reply
      and the VM saves the practice file. Keep the listener off the public
      interface.
    </p>
  </section>
</DemoLessonLayout>
